item0.id: 1
item0.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item0.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item0.difficulty: Medium
item0.question: A sales ops analyst needs to load 120,000 Opportunity Product updates with corrected prices. Which tool is most appropriate?
item0.type: single
item0.options[0]: Data Loader
item0.options[1]: Data Import Wizard
item0.options[2]: Report Export
item0.options[3]: Change Sets
item0.answers[0]: Data Loader
item0.explanation: Data Loader is designed for large-volume data operations (tens of thousands to millions of rows) and supports update/upsert with success and error logs, batch size control, and external IDs. The Data Import Wizard is browser-based and simpler but is intended for lower volumes and fewer objects, and it lacks some advanced matching/upsert options needed for complex line-item updates.

item1.id: 2
item1.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item1.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item1.difficulty: Medium
item1.question: A business user wants to quickly upload 8,000 Contacts from a CSV using a guided, browser-based experience with duplicate checks. What should the admin use?
item1.type: single
item1.options[0]: Data Import Wizard
item1.options[1]: Data Loader
item1.options[2]: Schema Builder
item1.options[3]: Workbench SOQL
item1.answers[0]: Data Import Wizard
item1.explanation: The Data Import Wizard runs entirely in the browser, supports standard objects like Accounts and Contacts, and includes built-in matching and duplicate prevention. It’s ideal for moderate volumes and non-admin users, while Data Loader is better for very high volumes or advanced mappings.

item2.id: 3
item2.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item2.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item2.difficulty: Hard
item2.question: Which two features help standardize and cleanse data before it’s saved?
item2.type: multiple
item2.options[0]: Validation Rules
item2.options[1]: Required fields on page layouts
item2.options[2]: Big Deal Alerts
item2.options[3]: List Views
item2.answers[0]: Validation Rules
item2.answers[1]: Required fields on page layouts
item2.explanation: Validation rules enforce business logic at save time (e.g., format checks, cross-field dependencies). Making fields required on page layouts forces users to provide core values during entry. Big Deal Alerts and List Views don’t clean data on save. 
item2.selectcount: 2

item3.id: 4
item3.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item3.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item3.difficulty: Medium
item3.question: Sales leadership wants a report to show Opportunities even if no Activities exist. What should the admin use?
item3.type: single
item3.options[0]: Custom Report Type with Opportunities as primary and Activities optional
item3.options[1]: Standard Activities report
item3.options[2]: Tabular report on Tasks
item3.options[3]: Joined report with two blocks
item3.answers[0]: Custom Report Type with Opportunities as primary and Activities optional
item3.explanation: Custom Report Types let you define the parent–child relationship and include parent records “with or without” related children. Selecting Opportunities as the primary object and Activities as an optional child ensures all Opportunities appear, even with zero Activities.

item4.id: 5
item4.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item4.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item4.difficulty: Medium
item4.question: A VP wants to segment Accounts into tiers directly in a report without changing data. What should the admin configure?
item4.type: single
item4.options[0]: Bucket field
item4.options[1]: Formula field on Account
item4.options[2]: Record Type
item4.options[3]: Compact Layout
item4.answers[0]: Bucket field
item4.explanation: Bucket fields create ad‑hoc groupings in the report layer (e.g., revenue ranges) with no schema changes. A formula field would permanently change the schema and require deployment; bucket fields keep it report-specific and easily editable.

item5.id: 6
item5.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item5.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item5.difficulty: Medium
item5.question: The company requires a monthly full data backup stored offline. Which native feature should be used?
item5.type: single
item5.options[0]: Data Export Service
item5.options[1]: Report subscription
item5.options[2]: Data Import Wizard
item5.options[3]: Dev Console Query
item5.answers[0]: Data Export Service
item5.explanation: The Data Export Service schedules comprehensive .zip exports of object data (including attachments if selected). Reports don’t capture all fields/objects, and the Import Wizard/Developer Console aren’t designed for backups.

item6.id: 7
item6.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item6.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item6.difficulty: Hard
item6.question: Which two tools can extract Salesforce data for analysis outside the platform?
item6.type: multiple
item6.options[0]: Data Loader
item6.options[1]: Data Export Service
item6.options[2]: Lightning App Builder
item6.options[3]: Path
item6.answers[0]: Data Loader
item6.answers[1]: Data Export Service
item6.explanation: Data Loader can query or export object data with filters; the Data Export Service produces scheduled full exports. App Builder and Path are presentation/UX tools, not extraction tools.
item6.selectcount: 2

item7.id: 8
item7.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item7.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item7.difficulty: Medium
item7.question: Users want to change dashboard results by industry without editing reports. What should the admin add?
item7.type: single
item7.options[0]: Dashboard filter
item7.options[1]: Joined report
item7.options[2]: Report row-level formula
item7.options[3]: Compact layout
item7.answers[0]: Dashboard filter
item7.explanation: Dashboard filters apply a consistent filter value across multiple components at view time, avoiding separate filtered reports and enabling self-service exploration.

item8.id: 9
item8.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item8.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item8.difficulty: Medium
item8.question: Sales managers should receive a summary report every Friday at 7 AM. What should the admin configure?
item8.type: single
item8.options[0]: Report subscription
item8.options[1]: Dashboard refresh
item8.options[2]: Data export
item8.options[3]: Field history tracking
item8.answers[0]: Report subscription
item8.explanation: Subscriptions deliver report results via email or notifications on a set schedule, optionally with conditions. Dashboard refreshes don’t proactively deliver the underlying report to inboxes.

item9.id: 10
item9.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item9.topic: Data and Analytics Management
item9.difficulty: Hard
item9.question: Which two report features help highlight outliers without changing underlying data?
item9.type: multiple
item9.options[0]: Conditional formatting
item9.options[1]: Row-level formulas
item9.options[2]: Profile login hours
item9.options[3]: Approval steps
item9.answers[0]: Conditional formatting
item9.answers[1]: Row-level formulas
item9.explanation: Conditional formatting visually flags thresholds (e.g., red for low margin). Row-level formulas compute derived values per row (e.g., variance) solely within the report—no schema changes required.
item9.selectcount: 2

item10.id: 11
item10.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item10.topic: Configuration and Setup
item10.difficulty: Easy
item10.question: Where can an admin configure company locale, fiscal year, and view org ID?
item10.type: single
item10.options[0]: Company Information
item10.options[1]: App Launcher
item10.options[2]: Report Settings
item10.options[3]: Lightning App Builder
item10.answers[0]: Company Information
item10.explanation: Company Information centralizes org-level settings like locale, fiscal year model, licenses, storage, and the org ID—foundational context for admins.

item11.id: 12
item11.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item11.topic: Configuration and Setup
item11.difficulty: Medium
item11.question: A contractor needs temporary access for 60 days. What should the admin do first?
item11.type: single
item11.options[0]: Create a user with an expiration-based freeze/removal process
item11.options[1]: Change the contractor’s role
item11.options[2]: Create a public group
item11.options[3]: Add to a queue
item11.answers[0]: Create a user with an expiration-based freeze/removal process
item11.explanation: Access starts with a user record (license, profile). For temporary users, plan deactivation or scheduled freeze to enforce least privilege and compliance timelines.

item12.id: 13
item12.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item12.topic: Configuration and Setup
item12.difficulty: Medium
item12.question: Which two settings can be enforced at the profile level?
item12.type: multiple
item12.options[0]: Login hours
item12.options[1]: Login IP ranges
item12.options[2]: Fiscal year model
item12.options[3]: Dashboard refresh schedule
item12.answers[0]: Login hours
item12.answers[1]: Login IP ranges
item12.explanation: Profiles govern authentication constraints per user group. Fiscal year and dashboard schedules are org/report configurations, not profile controls.
item12.selectcount: 2

item13.id: 14
item13.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item13.topic: Configuration and Setup
item13.difficulty: Medium
item13.question: A team member needs extra object permissions for a project without changing their base profile. What should the admin assign?
item13.type: single
item13.options[0]: Permission set
item13.options[1]: Role
item13.options[2]: Record type
item13.options[3]: Queue membership
item13.answers[0]: Permission set
item13.explanation: Permission sets layer additional object, field, and system permissions on top of a profile, supporting temporary or targeted privilege elevation without broadening the baseline profile.

item14.id: 15
item14.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item14.topic: Configuration and Setup
item14.difficulty: Hard
item14.question: Which two tasks are performed in Setup, not in the app UI?
item14.type: multiple
item14.options[0]: Create users
item14.options[1]: Configure object permissions
item14.options[2]: Post to a record feed
item14.options[3]: Create a task on an Opportunity
item14.answers[0]: Create users
item14.answers[1]: Configure object permissions
item14.explanation: Setup handles administrative configuration (user provisioning, permissioning). Posting to feeds and creating Tasks are end-user activities on records.
item14.selectcount: 2

item15.id: 16
item15.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item15.topic: Configuration and Setup
item15.difficulty: Easy
item15.question: Where can storage usage and license counts be reviewed?
item15.type: single
item15.options[0]: Company Information
item15.options[1]: Lightning Usage App
item15.options[2]: Path Settings
item15.options[3]: Object Manager
item15.answers[0]: Company Information
item15.explanation: Company Information provides at-a-glance license allocations and data/file storage consumption, crucial for capacity planning.

item16.id: 17
item16.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item16.topic: Configuration and Setup
item16.difficulty: Medium
item16.question: What action can an admin take directly from a user record to restore access?
item16.type: single
item16.options[0]: Reset password
item16.options[1]: Convert a lead
item16.options[2]: Create a campaign
item16.options[3]: Build a dashboard
item16.answers[0]: Reset password
item16.explanation: Admins can trigger a secure password reset from the user record, which sends a reset link and updates credentials without exposing the new password.

item17.id: 18
item17.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item17.topic: Configuration and Setup
item17.difficulty: Medium
item17.question: To ensure users only see the apps relevant to their job on the App Launcher, what should the admin configure?
item17.type: single
item17.options[0]: Profiles and permission sets
item17.options[1]: Roles and territories
item17.options[2]: Queues and public groups
item17.options[3]: Dashboards and folders
item17.answers[0]: Profiles and permission sets
item17.explanation: App and object visibility is principally controlled by profile/permission-set assignments. Roles and groups influence record sharing, not the app catalog.

item18.id: 19
item18.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item18.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item18.difficulty: Medium
item18.question: Sales wants to capture a new competitor field on Opportunities. What should the admin create?
item18.type: single
item18.options[0]: Custom field
item18.options[1]: Custom object
item18.options[2]: Custom tab only
item18.options[3]: New permission set group
item18.answers[0]: Custom field
item18.explanation: When extending an existing object’s data model, add a custom field. A new object adds complexity and is only appropriate if you need a separate lifecycle or relationships.

item19.id: 20
item19.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item19.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item19.difficulty: Medium
item19.question: Different business units require unique picklist values and different layouts on the same object. Which feature should be used?
item19.type: single
item19.options[0]: Record types
item19.options[1]: Roles
item19.options[2]: Queues
item19.options[3]: Compact layouts
item19.answers[0]: Record types
item19.explanation: Record types segment business processes, restrict picklist options per process, and allow layout assignment by profile, enabling tailored UI/UX per team.

item20.id: 21
item20.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item20.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item20.difficulty: Medium
item20.question: What controls which fields, sections, and related lists appear on a record page?
item20.type: single
item20.options[0]: Page layout
item20.options[1]: Role hierarchy
item20.options[2]: Public group
item20.options[3]: Forecast category
item20.answers[0]: Page layout
item20.explanation: Page layouts configure the form-level UI—fields, sections, buttons, and related lists—independent of data access rights.

item21.id: 22
item21.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item21.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item21.difficulty: Medium
item21.question: Which tool lets admins arrange components on Lightning record, home, and app pages?
item21.type: single
item21.options[0]: Lightning App Builder
item21.options[1]: Flow Builder
item21.options[2]: Schema Builder
item21.options[3]: Report Builder
item21.answers[0]: Lightning App Builder
item21.explanation: Lightning App Builder assembles pages from components (standard, custom, and AppExchange), supports dynamic visibility rules, and targets desktop/mobile form factors.

item22.id: 23
item22.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item22.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item22.difficulty: Medium
item22.question: Executives want key fields visible in the highlights panel across desktop and mobile. What should the admin configure?
item22.type: single
item22.options[0]: Compact layout
item22.options[1]: Sharing rule
item22.options[2]: Validation rule
item22.options[3]: Dashboard filter
item22.answers[0]: Compact layout
item22.explanation: Compact layouts define the small set of top fields shown in the highlights panel and header on mobile, improving glanceable context.

item23.id: 24
item23.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item23.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item23.difficulty: Hard
item23.question: Which two components are configurable on a Lightning record page?
item23.type: multiple
item23.options[0]: Related lists
item23.options[1]: Tabs and accordion sections
item23.options[2]: Session timeout
item23.options[3]: Password policy
item23.answers[0]: Related lists
item23.answers[1]: Tabs and accordion sections
item23.explanation: Related lists and layout containers are page-level components. Session timeout and password policy are org security settings managed elsewhere.
item23.selectcount: 2

item24.id: 25
item24.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item24.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item24.difficulty: Medium
item24.question: Detail records must be deleted when the parent is deleted, and roll-up summaries are required. Which relationship fits?
item24.type: single
item24.options[0]: Master-detail
item24.options[1]: Lookup
item24.options[2]: Hierarchical
item24.options[3]: External lookup
item24.answers[0]: Master-detail
item24.explanation: Master‑detail enforces tight coupling: child (detail) inherits ownership/sharing from master, supports roll-up summary fields, and cascades deletes automatically.

item25.id: 26
item25.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item25.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item25.difficulty: Medium
item25.question: A custom child record should remain after the Account is deleted. Which relationship should be used?
item25.type: single
item25.options[0]: Lookup
item25.options[1]: Master-detail
item25.options[2]: Indirect lookup only
item25.options[3]: External object
item25.answers[0]: Lookup
item25.explanation: Lookup relationships are loosely coupled and don’t cascade deletes by default, allowing the child record to persist independently.

item26.id: 27
item26.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item26.topic: Object Manager & Lightning App Builder
item26.difficulty: Hard
item26.question: Record types can directly control which two things?
item26.type: multiple
item26.options[0]: Available picklist values
item26.options[1]: Business processes
item26.options[2]: License count
item26.options[3]: Password complexity
item26.answers[0]: Available picklist values
item26.answers[1]: Business processes
item26.explanation: Record types tailor picklists and tie to distinct business processes (e.g., different sales processes). Licenses/passwords are unrelated org settings.
item26.selectcount: 2

item27.id: 28
item27.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item27.topic: Automation
item27.difficulty: Medium
item27.question: Which tool should admins use by default for declarative automation in 2025?
item27.type: single
item27.options[0]: Flow Builder
item27.options[1]: Workflow Rules
item27.options[2]: Apex Triggers
item27.options[3]: Matching Rules
item27.answers[0]: Flow Builder
item27.explanation: Flow Builder consolidates modern automation patterns (before/after record triggers, scheduled, screen flows) and is the recommended clicks-first approach over legacy Workflow Rules.

item28.id: 29
item28.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item28.topic: Automation
item28.difficulty: Hard
item28.question: You must set a default value on the triggering record and avoid additional DML. Which flow type is most efficient?
item28.type: single
item28.options[0]: Before-save record-triggered flow
item28.options[1]: After-save record-triggered flow
item28.options[2]: Screen flow
item28.options[3]: Scheduled-triggered flow
item28.answers[0]: Before-save record-triggered flow
item28.explanation: Before‑save flows run prior to the database commit and can update the same record in memory, minimizing DML and improving performance versus after‑save flows.

item29.id: 30
item29.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item29.topic: Automation
item29.difficulty: Medium
item29.question: Pricing changes must be approved by a regional manager before an Opportunity can close. What should the admin configure?
item29.type: single
item29.options[0]: Approval process
item29.options[1]: Auto-response rule
item29.options[2]: Territory model
item29.options[3]: Email-to-Case
item29.answers[0]: Approval process
item29.explanation: Approval processes route records to approvers based on criteria with locking, step logic, and tracked outcomes—purpose-built governance versus messaging or routing tools.

item30.id: 31
item30.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item30.topic: Automation
item30.difficulty: Hard
item30.question: Which two features can prevent users from saving records that violate business requirements?
item30.type: multiple
item30.options[0]: Validation rules
item30.options[1]: Required fields at the field level
item30.options[2]: Dashboard filters
item30.options[3]: Chatter recommendations
item30.answers[0]: Validation rules
item30.answers[1]: Required fields at the field level
item30.explanation: Validation rules enforce logical constraints; field-level “Required” ensures critical data capture. Dashboards/Chatter do not block saves.
item30.selectcount: 2

item31.id: 32
item31.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item31.topic: Automation
item31.difficulty: Medium
item31.question: Which flow type collects user input through guided screens?
item31.type: single
item31.options[0]: Screen flow
item31.options[1]: Before-save flow
item31.options[2]: Platform event-triggered flow
item31.options[3]: External change data capture flow
item31.answers[0]: Screen flow
item31.explanation: Screen flows render UI elements (inputs, choices, datatables) to guide users and can perform actions based on responses.

item32.id: 33
item32.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item32.topic: Automation
item32.difficulty: Medium
item32.question: A nightly job should evaluate Accounts for inactivity and create Tasks. Which flow type should be used?
item32.type: single
item32.options[0]: Scheduled-triggered flow
item32.options[1]: Screen flow
item32.options[2]: Approval process
item32.options[3]: Inbound change set
item32.answers[0]: Scheduled-triggered flow
item32.explanation: Scheduled flows process batches of records on a timetable without user interaction—perfect for recurring operational jobs.

item33.id: 34
item33.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item33.topic: Automation
item33.difficulty: Hard
item33.question: Which two actions are available in Flow Builder without code?
item33.type: multiple
item33.options[0]: Create or update records
item33.options[1]: Send email alerts
item33.options[2]: Change Salesforce edition
item33.options[3]: Disable org-wide defaults
item33.answers[0]: Create or update records
item33.answers[1]: Send email alerts
item33.explanation: Flows can perform DML and send notifications through Email Alert actions. Changing editions or OWDs are administrative tasks not executed by flow actions.
item33.selectcount: 2

item34.id: 35
item34.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item34.topic: Automation
item34.difficulty: Medium
item34.question: A flow that previously worked now fails after making a picklist field required. What should the admin check first?
item34.type: single
item34.options[0]: Flow error emails and debug logs to confirm missing required values
item34.options[1]: Forecast hierarchy
item34.options[2]: Dashboard running user
item34.options[3]: List view charts
item34.answers[0]: Flow error emails and debug logs to confirm missing required values
item34.explanation: Error emails/debug runs reveal which element failed and often point to unpopulated required fields. Fix by setting the new required field in the flow path.

item35.id: 36
item35.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item35.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item35.difficulty: Medium
item35.question: Which object tracks potential revenue, close date, and stage?
item35.type: single
item35.options[0]: Opportunity
item35.options[1]: Case
item35.options[2]: Campaign
item35.options[3]: Contract
item35.answers[0]: Opportunity
item35.explanation: Opportunities model sales deals with pipeline attributes (amount, stage, probability, close date) and drive forecasting and reporting.

item36.id: 37
item36.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item36.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item36.difficulty: Medium
item36.question: Which object represents an unqualified prospect prior to conversion?
item36.type: single
item36.options[0]: Lead
item36.options[1]: Contact
item36.options[2]: Case
item36.options[3]: Order
item36.answers[0]: Lead
item36.explanation: Leads capture early-stage prospects and can be converted to Account/Contact (and optionally Opportunity) once qualified.

item37.id: 38
item37.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item37.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item37.difficulty: Medium
item37.question: Marketing wants to measure responses from webinars and associate them to Opportunities. What should be used?
item37.type: single
item37.options[0]: Campaigns
item37.options[1]: Entitlements
item37.options[2]: Milestones
item37.options[3]: Assets
item37.answers[0]: Campaigns
item37.explanation: Campaigns track marketing initiatives and member responses; with Campaign Influence, they can attribute impact to Opportunities.

item38.id: 39
item38.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item38.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item38.difficulty: Hard
item38.question: Which two records are typically created automatically during lead conversion?
item38.type: multiple
item38.options[0]: Account
item38.options[1]: Contact
item38.options[2]: Case
item38.options[3]: Dashboard
item38.answers[0]: Account
item38.answers[1]: Contact
item38.explanation: Converting a Lead produces an Account and Contact; an Opportunity is optional. Cases/Dashboards are unrelated to conversion.
item38.selectcount: 2

item39.id: 40
item39.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item39.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item39.difficulty: Medium
item39.question: What object is used to add product lines and quantities to a deal?
item39.type: single
item39.options[0]: Opportunity Product
item39.options[1]: Case Team
item39.options[2]: Campaign Member
item39.options[3]: Contract Line Item
item39.answers[0]: Opportunity Product
item39.explanation: Opportunity Products (Line Items) tie Products/Pricebook Entries, quantities, and unit prices to a specific Opportunity for rollups.

item40.id: 41
item40.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item40.topic: Sales and Marketing Applications
item40.difficulty: Medium
item40.question: Which feature guides reps with key fields and stage-based coaching on Opportunities?
item40.type: single
item40.options[0]: Path
item40.options[1]: Queues
item40.options[2]: Entitlements
item40.options[3]: Public groups
item40.answers[0]: Path
item40.explanation: Path highlights critical fields and provides stage‑specific guidance so reps know what to complete at each step.

item41.id: 42
item41.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item41.topic: Service and Support Applications
item41.difficulty: Medium
item41.question: Which object tracks customer issues and resolutions for support teams?
item41.type: single
item41.options[0]: Case
item41.options[1]: Opportunity
item41.options[2]: Campaign
item41.options[3]: Solution
item41.answers[0]: Case
item41.explanation: Cases represent support requests with ownership, SLA tracking, escalation, and linkage to entitlements/knowledge.

item42.id: 43
item42.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item42.topic: Service and Support Applications
item42.difficulty: Medium
item42.question: How can incoming cases be routed automatically to the right queue or user?
item42.type: single
item42.options[0]: Case assignment rules
item42.options[1]: Validation rules
item42.options[2]: Email templates
item42.options[3]: Compact layouts
item42.answers[0]: Case assignment rules
item42.explanation: Assignment rules evaluate criteria (origin, priority, product, etc.) and assign the case to specific users or queues on creation.

item43.id: 44
item43.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item43.topic: Service and Support Applications
item43.difficulty: Hard
item43.question: Which two features help distribute and organize case workload?
item43.type: multiple
item43.options[0]: Queues
item43.options[1]: Omni-Channel routing
item43.options[2]: Campaign Influence
item43.options[3]: Joined reports
item43.answers[0]: Queues
item43.answers[1]: Omni-Channel routing
item43.explanation: Queues collect unowned work for teams; Omni‑Channel routes items in real time based on skills/capacity, improving SLA adherence.
item43.selectcount: 2

item44.id: 45
item44.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item44.topic: Service and Support Applications
item44.difficulty: Medium
item44.question: Agents need a searchable knowledge base of approved solutions. Which feature should be enabled?
item44.type: single
item44.options[0]: Knowledge
item44.options[1]: Entitlements
item44.options[2]: Opportunities
item44.options[3]: Path
item44.answers[0]: Knowledge
item44.explanation: Salesforce Knowledge stores structured articles with approval workflows, versioning, data categories, and channel access for agents and customers.

item45.id: 46
item45.exam: Salesforce Platform Administrator
item45.topic: Service and Support Applications
item45.difficulty: Medium
item45.question: Customers should log cases and view status through a branded portal. What should the admin use?
item45.type: single
item45.options[0]: Experience Cloud
item45.options[1]: Workflow Rules
item45.options[2]: Forecasting
item45.options[3]: Territory Management
